  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your options open. Don't commit to a 'Pung' early if it ruins a potential 'Chow' sequence. A hand made mostly of Chows is easier to complete but scores fewer points.\n\nEfficiency (Shanten): Calculate how many cards you are away from a complete hand. If you are 'Yi-Shanten' (1 card away), focus entirely on speed rather than high points.\n\nDefensive Discarding: If an opponent has revealed three Pungs of the same suit, never discard a card of that suit. You risk 'giving' them the winning card (Feeding the Dragon).",
